WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:12.322
Silvermane.
In charge of organize crime for 30 years.

2
00:00:12.346 --> 00:00:15.158
<i>Someone burned down his mansion
a couple of nights ago.</i>

3
00:00:15.182 --> 00:00:17.244
- Addison!
- You keep following me.

4
00:00:17.268 --> 00:00:18.662
it won't end the way you want it to.

5
00:00:18.686 --> 00:00:20.770
<i>This guy have superpowers? Like you?</i>

6
00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.584
Do me favor. Hold off on printing that.

7
00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:26.878
<i>I want to warn Donegal
before he gets himself killed.</i>

8
00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:28.338
That's enough of that.

9
00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:29.840
There's gonna be a free-for-all.

10
00:00:29.864 --> 00:00:31.842
The people could use a hero.

11
00:00:31.866 --> 00:00:33.468
I hope they find someone.

12
00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:36.304
I can't help but wonder
what Ruby would think.

13
00:00:36.328 --> 00:00:37.806
<i>I'm not that guy anymore.</i>

14
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.349
<i>Any chance</i>

15
00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:40.350
you know who this is?

16
00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:41.393
That's Cat Hardy.

17
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:43.061
<i>Star attraction over at The Alcove.</i>

18
00:00:43.085 --> 00:00:44.563
<i>Is there somewhere we can talk?</i>

19
00:00:44.587 --> 00:00:45.689
- It's business.
- Flint.

20
00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:46.732
<i>Despite what I do.</i>

21
00:00:46.756 --> 00:00:48.006
I don't enjoy hurting people.

22
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.157
- Don't hurt him.
- What the hell is this?

23
00:00:55.181 --> 00:00:57.617
- Just leave us alone. please.
<i>- When someone</i>

24
00:00:57.641 --> 00:00:58.702
tells you what they are.

25
00:00:58.726 --> 00:01:00.620
- you have to listen.
- And what is he?

26
00:01:00.644 --> 00:01:02.581
Retired.

27
00:01:02.605 --> 00:01:04.124
I came here to offer him a job.

28
00:01:04.148 --> 00:01:06.859
My friend you met last night
he's disappeared.

29
00:01:34.178 --> 00:01:35.280
You were saying Flint's your bodyguard.

30
00:01:35.304 --> 00:01:38.533
Yes. He protects me and he is loyal.

31
00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:40.076
Hard to find these days.

32
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.913
No kidding. I didn't marry my husband
for his looks.

33
00:01:42.937 --> 00:01:45.916
What else can you tell us?
Does he have family. friends?

34
00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.168
I don't know anything
about his personal life.

35
00:01:48.192 --> 00:01:49.693
I know his address.

36
00:01:50.778 --> 00:01:53.989
Are we gonna talk about the fact that
he turned into some kind of sand monster?

37
00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:57.076
What I know. she knows.

38
00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.222
It started about six months ago.

39
00:02:00.246 --> 00:02:02.224
Slow. at first.

40
00:02:02.248 --> 00:02:04.309
But it's been getting worse.

41
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:06.645
And he never remembers when it happens?

42
00:02:06.669 --> 00:02:08.313
He always remembers.

43
00:02:08.337 --> 00:02:11.214
Unless he gets clubbed in the head
with an iron girder.

44
00:02:12.341 --> 00:02:15.779
That's it? He turned into sand. That's
It was sand. right?

45
00:02:15.803 --> 00:02:17.364
Just seems like kind of. like. a big deal.

46
00:02:17.388 --> 00:02:20.367
So. do you have any clues
as to what's causing this to happen?

47
00:02:20.391 --> 00:02:21.910
You haven't given us much to go on.

48
00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.787
Isn't that what the money's for?

49
00:02:23.811 --> 00:02:25.413
You're an investigator.

50
00:02:25.437 --> 00:02:27.231
Investigate.

51
00:02:28.232 --> 00:02:30.168
You know. an artist
doesn't just paint with air.

52
00:02:30.192 --> 00:02:32.712
He needs a canvas. brushes. paint.

53
00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:35.131
Do you think I'm withholding
from you. Mr. Reilly?

54
00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:36.424
What if I said I did?

55
00:02:36.448 --> 00:02:37.759
I'd ask why you thought that.

56
00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:39.803
- I'd say a lifetime of experience.
- With clients?

57
00:02:39.827 --> 00:02:41.828
With… women.

58
00:02:43.289 --> 00:02:45.141
As fun as this little game is. I'm afraid

59
00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:47.561
I have other business to attend to.

60
00:02:47.585 --> 00:02:49.587
Get to painting. Mr. Reilly.

61
00:02:58.721 --> 00:03:00.031
What do you think?

62
00:03:00.055 --> 00:03:02.367
I think you might need a cold shower.

63
00:03:02.391 --> 00:03:03.893
I think I might need one.

64
00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.123
But you're right.

65
00:03:08.147 --> 00:03:09.875
She is hiding something.

66
00:03:09.899 --> 00:03:11.150
All the fun ones do.

67
00:03:11.817 --> 00:03:13.545
I'm gonna check out Flint's apartment.

68
00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:14.796
Why don't you do down to the Bu.

69
00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:17.507
Bureau of Criminal Records? Yeah.

70
00:03:17.531 --> 00:03:19.426
Been a while since we've had a real case.

71
00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:20.784
But it ain't been that long.

72
00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.286
Gonna meet a new supplier
at the docks tomorrow.

73
00:04:05.454 --> 00:04:06.890
Canadian.

74
00:04:06.914 --> 00:04:08.308
You didn't tell me that.

75
00:04:08.332 --> 00:04:09.750
I'm telling you now.

76
00:04:11.043 --> 00:04:14.731
It's not smart for you to go out in public
till we know who tried to take you out.

77
00:04:14.755 --> 00:04:16.483
I'll go where I want.

78
00:04:16.507 --> 00:04:19.152
With all due respect.
you don't pay me what you pay me

79
00:04:19.176 --> 00:04:21.112
for my charm or disposition.

80
00:04:21.136 --> 00:04:25.075
You pay me to keep you alive
and I'm telling you it's a bad idea.

81
00:04:25.099 --> 00:04:28.703
If you dying benefitted me.
I would have done it myself ten years ago.

82
00:04:28.727 --> 00:04:31.164
But I know what I'm good at.
I know what I'm not.

83
00:04:31.188 --> 00:04:34.084
and I need you to stay alive and in power.

84
00:04:34.108 --> 00:04:36.753
So. pretty please. with cherries on top.

85
00:04:36.777 --> 00:04:38.296
let me go down to the docks ahead of you.

86
00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.507
Once I make sure everything's kosher.
you can waltz on in

87
00:04:40.531 --> 00:04:42.533
and show everyone
the brightness of your feathers.

88
00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:45.035
You finished?

89
00:04:48.706 --> 00:04:50.433
Problem is not that the guy is out there.

90
00:04:50.457 --> 00:04:53.687
The problem is they thought
they could take me out at all.

91
00:04:53.711 --> 00:04:56.147
Ever since The Spider disappeared.

92
00:04:56.171 --> 00:04:58.108
things have been comfortable.

93
00:04:58.132 --> 00:05:01.236
Maybe someone's thinking
that I got complacent.

94
00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.761
Or soft.

95
00:05:03.679 --> 00:05:04.763
Maybe you're one of them.

96
00:05:06.557 --> 00:05:08.451
Thinking you could take me out.

97
00:05:08.475 --> 00:05:10.787
If you could set yourself on fire

98
00:05:10.811 --> 00:05:13.206
like Addison. then you might have a shot.

99
00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:16.459
Imagine controlling that kind of power.

100
00:05:16.483 --> 00:05:19.004
Now Flint goes missing.

101
00:05:19.028 --> 00:05:20.588
Right after.

102
00:05:20.612 --> 00:05:23.341
He's been acting strange lately.

103
00:05:23.365 --> 00:05:25.659
And if those two things are related...

104
00:05:26.577 --> 00:05:27.661
Go look for Flint.

105
00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:34.644
And when the boys find that PI...

106
00:05:34.668 --> 00:05:35.979
Reilly.

107
00:05:36.003 --> 00:05:37.504
Bring him straight to me.

108
00:07:34.705 --> 00:07:35.956
Great.

109
00:07:47.426 --> 00:07:48.486
<i>Hi. this is.</i>

110
00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.488
- Robbie Robertson calling.
<i>- Mr. Robertson.</i>

111
00:07:50.512 --> 00:07:53.825
<i>how many times do I have to tell you?
You're never getting your old job back.</i>

112
00:07:53.849 --> 00:07:56.870
Listen. I don't know if Walters
has seen my article in the Gazette.

113
00:07:56.894 --> 00:07:59.247
- but I just I.
<i>- Mr. Robertson. there's no point...</i>

114
00:07:59.271 --> 00:08:01.749
What I'm saying is I j
I-I just need to sit with him. that's all.

115
00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:04.377
<i>- Mr. Roberston. please. Mr. Robertson.</i>
- But if you-if you just...

116
00:08:04.401 --> 00:08:06.629
<i>- I'm going to hang up now.</i>
- You would just give me a chance to

117
00:08:06.653 --> 00:08:08.756
I'm onto something truly sensational!

118
00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.300
It's the biggest story in years.

119
00:08:10.324 --> 00:08:12.576
There hasn't been anything this big
since The Spider.

120
00:08:15.162 --> 00:08:17.998
I promise it'll be worth his while.

121
00:08:21.627 --> 00:08:23.462
<i>I'll see what I can do.</i>

122
00:08:25.422 --> 00:08:27.924
Thank you. Thank you.

123
00:08:29.092 --> 00:08:32.155
<i>Flint Marko?</i>

124
00:08:32.179 --> 00:08:34.282
<i>Got a delivery.</i>

125
00:08:34.306 --> 00:08:35.909
Anybody home?

126
00:08:35.933 --> 00:08:37.183
Come on...

127
00:09:21.812 --> 00:09:23.689
Flint.

128
00:09:27.526 --> 00:09:29.236
<i>Addison!</i>

129
00:09:32.864 --> 00:09:34.717
Flint.

130
00:09:34.741 --> 00:09:37.369
It's Winston.
Silvermane wants to talk to you.

131
00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:40.538
Gimme the keys.

132
00:09:52.551 --> 00:09:54.261
Check the bedroom.

133
00:10:46.855 --> 00:10:48.565
Nice place.

134
00:10:50.484 --> 00:10:53.171
Yeah. Bit fancy for my taste.

135
00:10:53.195 --> 00:10:56.341
And I got a pretty good idea why.

136
00:10:56.365 --> 00:10:57.449
Why?

137
00:10:58.325 --> 00:10:59.677
Let's go.

138
00:10:59.701 --> 00:11:01.220
You think he got a new lady?

139
00:11:01.244 --> 00:11:04.080
That why he ain't coming to poker lately?

140
00:11:19.888 --> 00:11:22.700
Janet. Long time.

141
00:11:22.724 --> 00:11:24.077
Thought you might've wised up
and quit the biz.

142
00:11:24.101 --> 00:11:25.953
No. not me. Hank.

143
00:11:25.977 --> 00:11:28.063
Sad to report I'm dumb as ever.

144
00:11:29.523 --> 00:11:31.501
Found this sitting outside.

145
00:11:31.525 --> 00:11:33.359
I didn't know if it belonged to anyone.

146
00:11:36.822 --> 00:11:38.925
Ooh.

147
00:11:38.949 --> 00:11:40.927
You know my wife
made me quit eating these.

148
00:11:40.951 --> 00:11:42.136
Okay. well. in that case...

149
00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:45.204
Hey! Last I checked. you ain't my wife.

150
00:11:46.957 --> 00:11:49.185
- Name?
- Flint Marko.

151
00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:50.978
All right. Be right back.

152
00:11:51.002 --> 00:11:52.438
Don't you dare touch that bag.

153
00:11:52.462 --> 00:11:54.797
It ain't a bribe if I don't get to eat it.

154
00:11:57.759 --> 00:11:59.761
Hey. Charlie. How you been?

155
00:12:03.056 --> 00:12:05.993
Quite the record. our Mr. Marko.

156
00:12:06.017 --> 00:12:09.330
Grew up in Brooklyn. Working class.
Came back with no prospects.

157
00:12:09.354 --> 00:12:11.582
Small crimes. then bigger ones.

158
00:12:11.606 --> 00:12:14.168
Arrest. arrest. arrest.

159
00:12:14.192 --> 00:12:16.129
Now an enforcer for.

160
00:12:16.153 --> 00:12:17.755
Silvermane.

161
00:12:17.779 --> 00:12:20.157
That Winston guy showed up
while I was at Flint's.

162
00:12:20.866 --> 00:12:23.326
- You hid in the closet?
- I hid in the closet.

163
00:12:25.078 --> 00:12:26.431
Meuse-Argonne.

164
00:12:26.455 --> 00:12:28.266
Didn't you fight there too?

165
00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.810
Yeah.
Was one of the biggest battles of the war.

166
00:12:30.834 --> 00:12:32.145
There were a million of us there.

167
00:12:32.169 --> 00:12:35.189
Hold on. Is that - Addison.

168
00:12:35.213 --> 00:12:36.732
Looks like they were in the war together.

169
00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:39.277
Is that what Cat is hiding from you?

170
00:12:39.301 --> 00:12:42.071
I bet she knew that Flint
had a friend with superpowers.

171
00:12:42.095 --> 00:12:44.907
I know. What I don't know
is why she didn't tell me.

172
00:12:44.931 --> 00:12:46.742
Probably thought
you wouldn't have taken the case.

173
00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:48.642
She would've been right.

174
00:13:24.304 --> 00:13:26.157
I don't think I've ever heard that one.

175
00:13:26.181 --> 00:13:27.992
I wouldn't think so.

176
00:13:28.016 --> 00:13:29.518
It's an original.

177
00:13:31.895 --> 00:13:34.189
Visited Flint's apartment today.

178
00:13:36.733 --> 00:13:38.252
This mean anything to you?

179
00:13:38.276 --> 00:13:40.546
I knew he was in the war.

180
00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:43.090
Hard to believe he was ever so young.

181
00:13:43.114 --> 00:13:44.884
What about this guy?

182
00:13:44.908 --> 00:13:46.469
You see him
this little guy. right over here?

183
00:13:46.493 --> 00:13:49.496
He ever come around The Alcove.
visit Marko?

184
00:13:50.956 --> 00:13:52.457
Can't say I've ever seen him.

185
00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:56.938
His name's... Addison.

186
00:13:56.962 --> 00:13:59.732
He's the guy that
burned down Silvermane's mansion.

187
00:13:59.756 --> 00:14:01.567
He's dead now.

188
00:14:01.591 --> 00:14:03.343
So's the PI that shot him.

189
00:14:03.927 --> 00:14:07.638
What can I say?
The world's a dangerous place.

190
00:14:12.102 --> 00:14:13.871
You're pretty cool under pressure.

191
00:14:13.895 --> 00:14:15.706
- I wasn't aware I was under any.
- Why didn't you tell me.

192
00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:18.459
- Flint worked for Silvermane?
- Would you have taken the case if I had?

193
00:14:18.483 --> 00:14:19.460
- I don't like surprises.
- I'll remember that

194
00:14:19.484 --> 00:14:21.152
when your birthday rolls around.

195
00:14:24.406 --> 00:14:26.425
The deed is under my name.

196
00:14:26.449 --> 00:14:29.512
but it's no secret
Silvermane owns this place.

197
00:14:29.536 --> 00:14:32.431
And Flint's a good way
to protect his investment.

198
00:14:32.455 --> 00:14:34.457
- And you.
- And me.

199
00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.854
You see. this club lives and dies
on people walking through that door

200
00:14:38.878 --> 00:14:40.839
because they want what I give them.

201
00:14:44.175 --> 00:14:46.070
You trying to get me. Mr. Reilly?

202
00:14:46.094 --> 00:14:47.989
"Get you"?

203
00:14:48.013 --> 00:14:49.657
Understand me.

204
00:14:49.681 --> 00:14:51.158
Seems you got my number.

205
00:14:51.182 --> 00:14:53.286
I've learned a lot of them over the years.

206
00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:55.663
O-one for every Tom. Dick and Harry?

207
00:14:55.687 --> 00:14:58.124
You're interesting.

208
00:14:58.148 --> 00:15:00.251
Yeah? How's that?

209
00:15:00.275 --> 00:15:03.671
Well. the other night when we met.
you called yourself a coward.

210
00:15:03.695 --> 00:15:06.048
But I think you're braver than you let on.

211
00:15:06.072 --> 00:15:08.467
You're good.

212
00:15:08.491 --> 00:15:10.720
In an obvious sort of way.

213
00:15:10.744 --> 00:15:12.597
I'm as subtle as the situation requires.

214
00:15:12.621 --> 00:15:15.016
You see. I have business with Silvermane

215
00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.101
and I have business with you. Mr. Reilly.

216
00:15:17.125 --> 00:15:18.936
One has nothing to do with the other.

217
00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:22.172
Now. have I said enough for you
to keep the money you came here to return?

218
00:15:23.256 --> 00:15:24.817
Or have I misjudged you?

219
00:15:24.841 --> 00:15:27.486
No I'll keep working the case.

220
00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.095
Not because I'm brave.

221
00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:31.532
Why. then?

222
00:15:31.556 --> 00:15:33.784
A singer's got to know all the numbers.

223
00:15:33.808 --> 00:15:37.186
Maybe a detective has just
got to know all the answers.

224
00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.849
It's...

225
00:16:38.873 --> 00:16:40.559
It.. Tai chi.

226
00:16:40.583 --> 00:16:42.269
Yeah. that's right. It's tai chi.

227
00:16:42.293 --> 00:16:43.771
It's. it's good.

228
00:16:43.795 --> 00:16:47.316
It's good for breathing and relaxation.

229
00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:48.757
I recommend it.

230
00:16:50.051 --> 00:16:52.363
We don't have the slightest clue
what you're talking about.

231
00:16:52.387 --> 00:16:53.972
We don't care. either.

232
00:17:01.938 --> 00:17:03.833
A toaster? Really?

233
00:17:03.857 --> 00:17:05.941
Gosh. I shouldn't have thrown it so hard.

234
00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:18.537
- Come on. Come on.
- Let's go for a ride.

235
00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.525
Mind telling me why I'm here?

236
00:17:29.549 --> 00:17:30.985
Silvermane wants to see you.

237
00:17:31.009 --> 00:17:33.612
I figured that. I'm asking why.

238
00:17:33.636 --> 00:17:35.489
We're not really the "why" guys.

239
00:17:35.513 --> 00:17:38.451
Maybe you wouldn't be here
if you didn't try ripping the boss off.

240
00:17:38.475 --> 00:17:39.827
Donegal.

241
00:17:39.851 --> 00:17:41.245
I didn't have anything

242
00:17:41.269 --> 00:17:42.455
to do with his little scheme.

243
00:17:42.479 --> 00:17:44.123
I actually tried to talk him out of it.

244
00:17:44.147 --> 00:17:46.751
Like I said. the boss just wants to talk.

245
00:17:46.775 --> 00:17:50.421
And I've got no idea who hired Addison
to burn down your boss' house.

246
00:17:50.445 --> 00:17:52.089
You don't know nothing?

247
00:17:52.113 --> 00:17:53.924
Double negative.
but we'll set that aside for now.

248
00:17:53.948 --> 00:17:55.634
My point is I'm not much of a detective.

249
00:17:55.658 --> 00:17:57.261
Yeah. then you got nothing to worry about.

250
00:17:57.285 --> 00:17:58.596
Just like Donegal. right?

251
00:17:58.620 --> 00:18:01.390
Yeah. just like Donegal.

252
00:18:01.414 --> 00:18:04.185
By the way. I am sorry about the nose.

253
00:18:04.209 --> 00:18:07.002
Me? That was him.

254
00:18:12.675 --> 00:18:14.511
Get out!

255
00:18:20.683 --> 00:18:22.244
Where'd he go?

256
00:18:22.268 --> 00:18:23.895
Check the side.

257
00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:32.421
The boss ain't gonna like this.

258
00:18:32.445 --> 00:18:34.447
Yeah. he wanted us to bring him in.

259
00:18:35.782 --> 00:18:37.593
Get in the car.

260
00:18:37.617 --> 00:18:39.118
Dumbass.

261
00:18:47.043 --> 00:18:49.063
<i>Times are tough all over.</i>

262
00:18:49.087 --> 00:18:51.941
But the true measure of a city

263
00:18:51.965 --> 00:18:54.735
is in how it responds to the hard times.

264
00:18:54.759 --> 00:18:58.155
And this isn't Topeka or Kalamazoo.

265
00:18:58.179 --> 00:18:59.657
This is New York.

266
00:18:59.681 --> 00:19:02.493
We're gonna link arms and stand strong

267
00:19:02.517 --> 00:19:05.162
against the rising tide.

268
00:19:05.186 --> 00:19:07.665
It was easy to stand up here
when the streets...

269
00:19:07.689 --> 00:19:10.042
What's the headline here?

270
00:19:10.066 --> 00:19:13.254
"Desperate Morris Delivers Dud."

271
00:19:13.278 --> 00:19:15.381
No. I'd-I'd go with quadruple M:

272
00:19:15.405 --> 00:19:17.550
"'Mayor's Missive Misses Mark."

273
00:19:17.574 --> 00:19:19.134
Man. I wouldn't trust Hudson

274
00:19:19.158 --> 00:19:22.304
to do my laundry and that man's
gonna beat Morris by ten points.

275
00:19:22.328 --> 00:19:25.808
Sometimes you just
want a different brand of snake oil.

276
00:19:25.832 --> 00:19:29.311
So. you gonna explain your face?

277
00:19:29.335 --> 00:19:32.171
Let's just say you should
lay off the Addison reporting.

278
00:19:33.423 --> 00:19:34.984
Silvermane?

279
00:19:35.008 --> 00:19:38.070
He's on a warpath about Addison.
Wants to know who's coming after him.

280
00:19:38.094 --> 00:19:40.614
So tread... lightly.

281
00:19:40.638 --> 00:19:44.118
Man. I'm not the one with a face
that looks like hamburger meat.

282
00:19:44.142 --> 00:19:46.328
I've tangoed with his guys before.

283
00:19:46.352 --> 00:19:48.831
As the man with the mask and the goggles.

284
00:19:48.855 --> 00:19:51.625
New York's beloved hero of the hour.

285
00:19:51.649 --> 00:19:53.294
Not as Ben Reilly.

286
00:19:53.318 --> 00:19:54.795
You know what? Gimme that.

287
00:19:54.819 --> 00:19:56.881
I'm making a declaration right now.

288
00:19:56.905 --> 00:19:58.674
That's right.

289
00:19:58.698 --> 00:20:00.843
If I'm re-elected

290
00:20:00.867 --> 00:20:02.928
you can say goodbye to Prohibition.

291
00:20:02.952 --> 00:20:04.680
Man knows his audience.

292
00:20:04.704 --> 00:20:08.540
As God is my witness.
you'll never go thirsty again.

293
00:20:10.043 --> 00:20:13.147
Look. all I'm saying
is you're in it with Silvermane now.

294
00:20:13.171 --> 00:20:15.524
If the choice is to suit up or die.

295
00:20:15.548 --> 00:20:17.276
might be time to tango again.

296
00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.778
Maybe you'd be doing the city a favor
in the process.

297
00:20:19.802 --> 00:20:22.239
Come on. Robbie. Enough of that.

298
00:20:22.263 --> 00:20:23.657
You know what I'm doing after this?

299
00:20:23.681 --> 00:20:25.534
- What?
- Being beautiful.

300
00:20:25.558 --> 00:20:28.704
And working the Addison story.

301
00:20:28.728 --> 00:20:31.314
I don't publish. I don't eat. my friend.

302
00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:35.652
I've been thinking about the Canadians.

303
00:20:36.903 --> 00:20:38.380
You gonna let me handle it?

304
00:20:38.404 --> 00:20:40.925
No. I'll do it.

305
00:20:40.949 --> 00:20:43.302
Plan stands. but...

306
00:20:43.326 --> 00:20:45.995
go ahead of me. Scout it out.

307
00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.480
I think it's stylish.

308
00:20:54.504 --> 00:20:56.089
What do you think. Winston?

309
00:20:57.173 --> 00:20:58.734
I'm not one for fashion.

310
00:20:58.758 --> 00:21:01.403
But the whole thing is a little...

311
00:21:01.427 --> 00:21:02.988
tired.

312
00:21:03.012 --> 00:21:06.182
Now. Winston.
have you got a gripe with her?

313
00:21:07.475 --> 00:21:11.311
No. I just think there's better things
to spend time on than dressing up dolls.

314
00:21:12.397 --> 00:21:14.833
Well. there's fashion and there's taste.

315
00:21:14.857 --> 00:21:18.587
Box it up. You like it too. right?

316
00:21:18.611 --> 00:21:19.797
Honestly. I think it's.

317
00:21:19.821 --> 00:21:21.531
Yeah. yeah. it's perfect.

318
00:21:40.091 --> 00:21:42.719
Excuse me. ma'am.
I'm looking for the Addisons.

319
00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:57.191
Mrs. Addison?

320
00:22:28.181 --> 00:22:29.682
Who are you?

321
00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:37.207
- Hey. brother.
- Don't "hey. brother" me.

322
00:22:37.231 --> 00:22:38.834
I asked you a question.

323
00:22:38.858 --> 00:22:40.127
You sure did.

324
00:22:40.151 --> 00:22:43.005
and seeing as you are a very large

325
00:22:43.029 --> 00:22:44.548
and angry man.

326
00:22:44.572 --> 00:22:45.799
I'm gonna answer.

327
00:22:45.823 --> 00:22:47.634
I'm looking for Vera Addison.

328
00:22:47.658 --> 00:22:49.595
Know where she is?

329
00:22:49.619 --> 00:22:50.971
Why do you want to know?

330
00:22:50.995 --> 00:22:52.848
Well. I am a reporter.

331
00:22:52.872 --> 00:22:54.975
Working a story on James Addison's death.

332
00:22:54.999 --> 00:22:57.418
Wanted to talk to his widow.

333
00:23:00.171 --> 00:23:01.672
Jimmy's dead?

334
00:23:04.217 --> 00:23:06.677
I'm sorry. You... you guys were friends?

335
00:23:07.845 --> 00:23:09.347
How did he die?

336
00:23:10.431 --> 00:23:11.933
There was an explosion...

337
00:23:13.976 --> 00:23:16.246
at the Standard Oil depot.

338
00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:17.998
Why are you writing about him?

339
00:23:18.022 --> 00:23:21.168
Well. before he died
he burned down the wrong house.

340
00:23:21.192 --> 00:23:22.753
Whose?

341
00:23:22.777 --> 00:23:24.278
Silvermane.

342
00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:33.806
- Think it's time for you to leave.
- Wait. wait.

343
00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:35.432
wait. wait. wait. wait. wait.
wait. wait. wait. wait.

344
00:23:35.456 --> 00:23:37.309
Addison didn't just take it

345
00:23:37.333 --> 00:23:40.270
upon himself to burn down the house
of the most dangerous man in the city.

346
00:23:40.294 --> 00:23:42.022
Someone paid him to do it.

347
00:23:42.046 --> 00:23:45.567
Now. look. he was your friend.
so I'm guessing he wasn't a bad guy.

348
00:23:45.591 --> 00:23:47.111
He was sick.

349
00:23:47.135 --> 00:23:50.656
And these days call for men
to use their sicknesses to get by.

350
00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:53.117
Until their sicknesses eat them alive.

351
00:23:53.141 --> 00:23:55.941
- Hang on. what do you mean. he was sick?
- I don't know who hired him.

352
00:23:57.061 --> 00:23:58.789
But. yeah.

353
00:23:58.813 --> 00:24:00.332
his wife might.

354
00:24:00.356 --> 00:24:02.042
And do you know where I can find her?

355
00:24:02.066 --> 00:24:03.794
Try the Geoffrey Hotel.

356
00:24:03.818 --> 00:24:05.921
She always went there
when they came into some money.

357
00:24:05.945 --> 00:24:07.631
And when she came back.

358
00:24:07.655 --> 00:24:09.258
the money was gone.

359
00:24:09.282 --> 00:24:10.968
Go figure.

360
00:24:10.992 --> 00:24:13.303
Well. thanks.

361
00:24:13.327 --> 00:24:14.829
I'll pay her a visit.

362
00:24:17.832 --> 00:24:19.935
I told you.

363
00:24:19.959 --> 00:24:21.895
he hardly comes to the office anymore.

364
00:24:21.919 --> 00:24:23.856
I can't remember the last time I saw him.

365
00:24:23.880 --> 00:24:27.192
Well. maybe this'll jog your memory.

366
00:24:27.216 --> 00:24:29.217
Please! I'm telling you the truth.

367
00:24:31.304 --> 00:24:33.574
For your sake. I hope so.

368
00:24:33.598 --> 00:24:35.348
We'll be back.

369
00:24:50.489 --> 00:24:51.466
Janet!

370
00:24:51.490 --> 00:24:53.159
Did they hurt you?

371
00:24:54.368 --> 00:24:57.621
No. not this time.
But they said they'd be back.

372
00:24:58.915 --> 00:25:01.351
Ben. they put a gun to my head.

373
00:25:01.375 --> 00:25:03.312
They kept saying that
I'd end up like Donegal?

374
00:25:03.336 --> 00:25:05.856
That if I didn't tell them where you were.

375
00:25:05.880 --> 00:25:08.859
he and I'd be crossing
the River Styx together.

376
00:25:08.883 --> 00:25:10.718
What does that mean?

377
00:25:11.969 --> 00:25:13.864
It means Donegal's dead.

378
00:25:13.888 --> 00:25:15.949
Silvermane killed him.

379
00:25:15.973 --> 00:25:17.910
But I'll take care of it.

380
00:25:17.934 --> 00:25:21.705
Ever since Ruby died. I've been waiting
for you to get it back together.

381
00:25:21.729 --> 00:25:25.000
Back to the man I know
is buried somewhere inside you.

382
00:25:25.024 --> 00:25:26.692
Five years.

383
00:25:28.236 --> 00:25:29.946
And this is how it ends.

384
00:25:31.030 --> 00:25:32.549
Janet.

385
00:25:32.573 --> 00:25:34.259
Go home. Get-get some rest.

386
00:25:34.283 --> 00:25:36.911
You'll feel better and I'll…
I'll call you when it's safe.

387
00:25:37.995 --> 00:25:39.497
Yeah. I'm gonna go home.

388
00:25:41.207 --> 00:25:42.768
But I am not coming back.

389
00:25:42.792 --> 00:25:45.520
I care about you. Ben.

390
00:25:45.544 --> 00:25:47.046
so deeply.

391
00:25:48.297 --> 00:25:50.299
But not enough to die for you.

392
00:25:51.509 --> 00:25:52.718
Janet...

393
00:25:53.803 --> 00:25:56.305
Janet!

394
00:26:44.478 --> 00:26:46.290
Hiya! I'm Pete with Maintenance.

395
00:26:46.314 --> 00:26:48.125
Sorry about the leak. It'll be no problem.

396
00:26:48.149 --> 00:26:50.377
I'll just Gosh. the unit downstairs.

397
00:26:50.401 --> 00:26:52.379
big mess. Water. water everywhere.

398
00:26:52.403 --> 00:26:54.089
- What's going on?
- Something about a leak?

399
00:26:54.113 --> 00:26:56.967
I like what you've done with place.
Although if you move the table

400
00:26:56.991 --> 00:27:00.512
over by the window.
you really get that sunset glow at dinner.

401
00:27:00.536 --> 00:27:02.973
- I told you that.
- I'm sorry. have you been here before?

402
00:27:02.997 --> 00:27:06.834
I am familiar with the unit. yes.
Bathroom's that way?

403
00:27:25.978 --> 00:27:28.373
Well. don't just stand there.
Say something.

404
00:27:28.397 --> 00:27:31.484
Sir. w-what exactly are you fixing?

405
00:27:32.318 --> 00:27:34.296
Yep. yeah. I found the issue.

406
00:27:34.320 --> 00:27:36.965
You've got a busted Gerry casket.

407
00:27:36.989 --> 00:27:38.925
It's a misalignment

408
00:27:38.949 --> 00:27:41.285
from the mission joist.

409
00:28:03.516 --> 00:28:05.726
Excuse me.
w-what's happening in there?

410
00:28:06.894 --> 00:28:09.397
Bit of an existential crisis. if I'm honest.

411
00:28:11.190 --> 00:28:13.025
About my toilet?

412
00:28:29.959 --> 00:28:31.794
I don't think that guy was a plumber.

413
00:28:54.024 --> 00:28:55.651
Stairs are to the left.

414
00:28:57.319 --> 00:28:58.821
Thanks for your trouble.

415
00:29:00.823 --> 00:29:02.616
Thanks for the dollar.

416
00:29:04.910 --> 00:29:06.745
Mrs. Addison?

417
00:29:09.290 --> 00:29:10.851
I didn't order anything.

418
00:29:10.875 --> 00:29:13.520
My name is Robbie Robertson.
I'm a reporter.

419
00:29:13.544 --> 00:29:17.065
Hold-hold ho-hold on.
hold on now. I just...

420
00:29:17.089 --> 00:29:18.650
- I just want to talk.
- You got three seconds

421
00:29:18.674 --> 00:29:20.735
to get out of here or I'm gonna scream.

422
00:29:20.759 --> 00:29:22.571
And I don't think you want
a white woman screaming

423
00:29:22.595 --> 00:29:25.097
about a Black man trying
to force his way into her hotel room.

424
00:29:26.682 --> 00:29:28.952
Actually. I got a hunch...

425
00:29:28.976 --> 00:29:31.329
that you wouldn't want
the city's most ruthless gangster

426
00:29:31.353 --> 00:29:35.167
knowing that the money someone
paid your husband to kill him

427
00:29:35.191 --> 00:29:37.252
was being spent on...

428
00:29:37.276 --> 00:29:40.297
lobster and designer clothes.

429
00:29:40.321 --> 00:29:43.341
So. go ahead and scream. honey.
Unless you want me to do it.

430
00:29:43.365 --> 00:29:45.950
I got a pretty deep voice. It really carries.

431
00:30:08.516 --> 00:30:10.076
<i>So. that's it?</i>

432
00:30:10.100 --> 00:30:11.912
What do you mean?

433
00:30:11.936 --> 00:30:15.081
No tears?
I just told you your husband died.

434
00:30:15.105 --> 00:30:17.316
People grieve in different ways.

435
00:30:19.109 --> 00:30:21.278
You already knew.

436
00:30:22.780 --> 00:30:26.343
James was a lot of things.
but not the type to cut and run.

437
00:30:26.367 --> 00:30:29.763
When he didn't come home that night.
I figured he was never coming home.

438
00:30:29.787 --> 00:30:32.557
- When did he start setting fires?
- Six months ago.

439
00:30:32.581 --> 00:30:35.268
Suddenly discovered
he had an innate talent for it.

440
00:30:35.292 --> 00:30:36.919
Who hired him for the Silvermane job?

441
00:30:38.170 --> 00:30:41.358
Just because I didn't scream
doesn't mean I'm an open book.

442
00:30:41.382 --> 00:30:43.485
As far as I'm concerned.

443
00:30:43.509 --> 00:30:46.177
James dug his own grave
and now he's lying in it.

444
00:31:02.820 --> 00:31:04.714
This place feels haunted.

445
00:31:04.738 --> 00:31:06.532
That's 'cause it is.

446
00:31:08.576 --> 00:31:10.911
Speaking of ghosts...

447
00:31:12.496 --> 00:31:14.015
Jimmy Addison's dead.

448
00:31:14.039 --> 00:31:15.541
What?

449
00:31:16.709 --> 00:31:17.936
When?

450
00:31:17.960 --> 00:31:20.146
Couple days ago.
Some reporter came around

451
00:31:20.170 --> 00:31:23.423
asking about him. Wanted to know
who hired him to kill Silvermane.

452
00:31:27.094 --> 00:31:28.154
You didn't know.

453
00:31:28.178 --> 00:31:30.598
If I'd known. I would have stopped him.

454
00:31:39.106 --> 00:31:40.625
Flint.

455
00:31:40.649 --> 00:31:42.109
You don't look so good.

456
00:31:43.193 --> 00:31:45.380
It happened again.

457
00:31:45.404 --> 00:31:47.340
I changed completely this time.

458
00:31:47.364 --> 00:31:49.009
Never changed back.

459
00:31:49.033 --> 00:31:50.784
Not all the way.

460
00:31:52.202 --> 00:31:54.121
It's like the doc said.

461
00:31:55.289 --> 00:31:56.957
Our clocks are ticking.

462
00:31:58.751 --> 00:32:00.604
Faster and faster now.

463
00:32:00.628 --> 00:32:02.504
Everything we went through.

464
00:32:05.215 --> 00:32:07.652
We deserve better. you and I.

465
00:32:07.676 --> 00:32:09.237
Let's get out of here.

466
00:32:09.261 --> 00:32:11.323
You can crash at my place.

467
00:32:11.347 --> 00:32:14.015
Better for us to stick together right now.

468
00:32:15.976 --> 00:32:17.645
Yeah.

469
00:32:18.520 --> 00:32:21.833
You have to check every crate?
Is it 'cause we're Canadians?

470
00:32:21.857 --> 00:32:24.252
Yeah. it's 'cause you're Canadian. No.

471
00:32:24.276 --> 00:32:27.130
Boss doesn't trust anyone.
Myself included.

472
00:32:27.154 --> 00:32:29.966
That's why he still runs this town.

473
00:32:29.990 --> 00:32:31.801
Shipment's good. boss.

474
00:32:31.825 --> 00:32:33.219
Ready for you to come.

475
00:32:33.243 --> 00:32:35.703
<i>Right. I'm on my way.</i>

476
00:33:07.736 --> 00:33:09.947
What is that?

477
00:33:16.286 --> 00:33:17.806
Hey. go check it out.

478
00:33:17.830 --> 00:33:20.123
Go. Go. go. go. go. go!

479
00:33:21.208 --> 00:33:23.167
He's on the roof! Aah!

480
00:33:27.965 --> 00:33:28.965
Shoot him!

481
00:33:40.269 --> 00:33:41.645
Hello.

482
00:34:00.873 --> 00:34:02.124
Where'd he go?

483
00:34:09.923 --> 00:34:11.133
That way.

484
00:34:13.761 --> 00:34:15.220
Come here!

485
00:34:16.263 --> 00:34:17.765
Thank you.

486
00:34:18.724 --> 00:34:20.142
God.

487
00:34:21.143 --> 00:34:22.519
Don't you ever run out of bullets?

488
00:34:23.228 --> 00:34:24.729
Guess you do.

489
00:34:34.239 --> 00:34:36.825
What? What the hell are you waiting for?

490
00:34:37.910 --> 00:34:39.471
After you.

491
00:34:39.495 --> 00:34:41.431
No. no. By all means.

492
00:34:41.455 --> 00:34:42.747
Out of the car!

493
00:34:52.132 --> 00:34:54.009
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa! Not another step.

494
00:34:58.138 --> 00:35:00.015
See? Tai chi.

495
00:35:12.402 --> 00:35:14.756
- It's been a while.
- You've done well

496
00:35:14.780 --> 00:35:17.050
without me around. haven't you?

497
00:35:17.074 --> 00:35:19.219
Didn't know you did hit jobs now.

498
00:35:19.243 --> 00:35:22.597
- Do you mind if I ask you who hired you?
- Nobody hires me.

499
00:35:22.621 --> 00:35:24.456
I'm here because of Ben Reilly.

500
00:35:25.415 --> 00:35:28.812
- Reilly? The flatfoot?
- Yeah. that's right. I owe him a favor.

501
00:35:28.836 --> 00:35:30.563
Sorry. where are my manners?

502
00:35:30.587 --> 00:35:32.941
- Do you want a drink?
- No. I want you and your goons

503
00:35:32.965 --> 00:35:34.484
to lay off Reilly.

504
00:35:34.508 --> 00:35:36.402
He doesn't know who tried to kill you

505
00:35:36.426 --> 00:35:39.906
and roughing up his secretary
isn't gonna change that.

506
00:35:39.930 --> 00:35:43.117
So. I leave the gumshoe alone.
and that's it?

507
00:35:43.141 --> 00:35:45.078
'Cause. you know.
back in the day you really

508
00:35:45.102 --> 00:35:48.581
- couldn't leave me alone. could you?
- I don't think you're listening to me.

509
00:35:48.605 --> 00:35:50.416
Silvermane.

510
00:35:50.440 --> 00:35:52.335
This is your only warning.

511
00:35:52.359 --> 00:35:53.711
If you mess with Reilly

512
00:35:53.735 --> 00:35:55.237
or any of his people…

513
00:35:56.989 --> 00:35:58.490
I will kill you.

514
00:36:49.416 --> 00:36:50.393
Reilly.

515
00:36:50.417 --> 00:36:52.604
This you? This your doing?

516
00:36:52.628 --> 00:36:54.147
What are you talking about?

517
00:36:54.171 --> 00:36:56.441
<i>Did you stop Silvermane's car?</i>

518
00:36:56.465 --> 00:36:57.859
You heard about that?

519
00:36:57.883 --> 00:36:59.611
<i>Yeah. well. I got some bad news for you.</i>

520
00:36:59.635 --> 00:37:01.988
<i>Cops had an ambush
set up for Silvermane at the docks.</i>

521
00:37:02.012 --> 00:37:04.198
<i>Someone gave them a tip
about a booze exchange.</i>

522
00:37:04.222 --> 00:37:07.452
Someone tipped off the cops
about a Silvermane booze exchange?

523
00:37:07.476 --> 00:37:09.787
Yeah. they're rounding up
about a dozen of his guys right now.

524
00:37:09.811 --> 00:37:11.664
Cops were all set to catch
the man himself in the act.

525
00:37:11.688 --> 00:37:13.249
But Silvermane never showed.

526
00:37:13.273 --> 00:37:15.793
Do they know why he didn't show?

527
00:37:15.817 --> 00:37:19.589
<i>No. don't worry. Police got word that
someone stopped Silvermane from coming.</i>

528
00:37:19.613 --> 00:37:21.174
<i>They don't know it was you.</i>

529
00:37:21.198 --> 00:37:24.158
Shit. got to go.
I ain't trying to die in no phone booth.

530
00:37:50.852 --> 00:37:52.854
What the hell did I just do?
